      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SINGLES MOMENT (5) poses a serious threat, also moving up from BM62 after a solid fourth at Warrnambool on heavy ground and enjoying weight relief. His close Hamilton trial adds to his fitness, and the Dabernig stable has a strong track profile. CHILLI REAPER (7) is in superb form, finishing third in a Balaklava BM60 behind So Polite, just a length away, after a strong-closing second at Murray Bridge in a BM56 where she faced running issues. Though stepping up to BM66, she's race fit, lighter, has Jacob Opperman back, and won her only start here. GUSTY WAY (1) ran well, finishing seventh in a Morphettville BM70, beaten two and a half lengths, and faces an easier field after his Naracoorte win over Streetcar Fury. ONE BOUND (6) returns from five months off, bringing potential from a close second at Casterton BM62, and a Hamilton trial win sets him up well for this fresh run.",
